# K0 batch 10: regions r444-r470 (protocol v1.2.1)
# r444-r459 .claude/skills/security-scan/SKILL.md
SPLIT R:RULE-K0-0278 | a: A security scan is an evidence-based static review, not a penetration test; state its limitations in the report. | b: Name security-sensitive workflows as threat-modeling or manual-review candidates instead of claiming the scan proves them secure.
CX X:BF-K0-0008@16-16 | Every security report states that the scan is an evidence-based static review, not a penetration test, and cannot prove the application secure (reported as required even for a narrow verified issue).
SD P:EXTRA-K0-0209 R:RULE-K0-0278#a X:BF-K0-0008 | S: security-scan reports M: MUST (P, R), X no modality E: none in any T: every report | labels: P EXTRA, R ORACLE_LINKED (whole record)
SPLIT R:RULE-K0-0277 | a: Report concrete security risks, not generic advice. | b: Evaluate findings against actual exposure and application behavior, not mechanical pattern matches. | c: Never invent exploitability the code does not establish.
SD P:RULE-K0-0511 R:RULE-K0-0277#a | S: security findings M: MUST both E: none in either T: none
SD P:RULE-K0-0512 R:RULE-K0-0277#b | S: security findings M: MUST both E: none in either T: none
SPLIT P:RULE-K0-0521 | a: Label uncertain findings NEEDS VERIFICATION instead of presenting them as confirmed. | b: Never invent exploitability the code does not establish.
SD P:RULE-K0-0521#b R:RULE-K0-0277#c | S: security findings M: MUST (P record) = MUST + 'never' (R) (F7) E: none in either T: none
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-K0-0277#b P:RULE-K0-0525 | P (DEFINITION): normal LINQ predicates with user input are not SQL injection.
SPLIT R:RULE-K0-0276 | a: Confirmed findings are separated from NEEDS VERIFICATION items. | b: Security severity comes from exploitability, reachability, exposure, impact and context, never from a suspicious pattern, raw CVSS score or OWASP category alone. | c: A theoretical missing limit is not automatically High. | d: Findings carry severity, location, title, evidence, risk, impact, remediation and OWASP category when applicable.
SPLIT P:RULE-K0-0513 | a: Distinguish confirmed findings from items needing verification. | b: Assign severity from exploitability, reachability, impact and context, never from a suspicious pattern or raw CVSS alone.
SD P:RULE-K0-0513#a P:RULE-K0-0521#a R:RULE-K0-0276#a | S: security findings M: MUST (all) E: none in any T: none
RD DETAIL_DIFFERENCE R:RULE-K0-0276#b P:RULE-K0-0513#b | R adds 'or OWASP category alone' (from another cited location).
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-K0-0276#b P:RULE-K0-0519 | P: the severity factors; never convert advisory CVSS directly.
RD EXAMPLE_GENERAL R:RULE-K0-0120 P:RULE-K0-0514 | P: real secrets in Development files are not suppressed.
SPLIT R:RULE-K0-0282 | a: Recommend the smallest secure change consistent with the architecture. | b: Do not require mechanisms the project does not need. | c: Do not require a new authentication system unnecessarily, custom cryptography or [Authorize] on every action under a protecting global policy. | d: Do not recommend blanket encryption, security libraries merely to satisfy the scan, or disabling functionality a scanner cannot understand.
SPLIT P:EXTRA-K0-0216 | a: Recommend the smallest secure change consistent with the architecture. | b: Do not recommend blanket encryption of all fields, security libraries merely to satisfy the scan, or disabling functionality a static scanner cannot understand.
SD P:EXTRA-K0-0216#a R:RULE-K0-0282#a | S: security remediation M: MUST_NOT (P record) / MUST NOT (R record) both E: none in either T: none | labels: P EXTRA (whole record), R ORACLE_LINKED (whole record)
SD P:RULE-K0-0515 R:RULE-K0-0282#b | S: security remediation M: MUST_NOT both E: none in either T: none
SD P:EXTRA-K0-0216#b R:RULE-K0-0282#d | S: security remediation M: MUST_NOT both E: none in either T: none | labels: P EXTRA (whole record), R ORACLE_LINKED (whole record)
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-K0-0282#c P:RULE-K0-0156 | P: avoid redundant [Authorize] under a secure global policy.
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-K0-0282#c P:RULE-K0-0160 | P: no custom cryptography.
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-K0-0095 P:RULE-K0-0516 | P: evaluate effective authorization including global and fallback policies.
SPLIT R:RULE-K0-0279 | a: The review does not depend on a specific MCP server, agent, analyzer, commercial scanner or other external tool; tooling is evidence, not the sole authority. | b: Scanner reports are confirmed against the code before reporting with appropriate confidence.
SD P:RULE-K0-0517 R:RULE-K0-0279#a | S: security tooling M: MUST_NOT both E: none in either T: none
SD P:RULE-K0-0518 R:RULE-K0-0279#b | S: scanner reports M: MUST (P); R record MUST NOT, the part states the same obligation (F7) E: none in either T: before reporting
SPLIT R:RULE-K0-0280 | a: Inspect which surfaces exist and skip irrelevant checks instead of reporting them as failures. | b: A full pre-release or requested audit reviews every applicable layer; a targeted change starts with affected layers and expands across security boundaries.
SD P:EXTRA-K0-0210 R:RULE-K0-0280#a | S: security scan scope M: MUST both E: none in either T: none | labels: P EXTRA, R ORACLE_LINKED (whole record)
SD P:EXTRA-K0-0211 R:RULE-K0-0280#b | S: security scan scope M: MUST both E: none in either T: none | labels: P EXTRA, R ORACLE_LINKED (whole record)
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-K0-0123 P:RULE-K0-0520 | P (DEFINITION): route guards and hidden buttons are not automatically safe.
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-K0-0120 P:RULE-K0-0520 | P (DEFINITION): secrets in appsettings.Development.json are not automatically safe.
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-K0-0126 P:RULE-K0-0520 | P (DEFINITION): sensitive values logged at Debug are not automatically safe.
RD OVERLAP R:RULE-K0-0100 P:RULE-K0-0520 | P (DEFINITION): CORS as an authorization substitute is not safe.
SPLIT X:BF-K0-0009 | a@82-82: Every confirmed finding includes severity, file/location, title, evidence, why it is a risk, likely impact, smallest remediation and OWASP category when applicable. | b@132-132: Layer status is PASS, FINDINGS, NOT APPLICABLE or NOT CHECKED; never PASS for an uninspected layer.
SD P:EXTRA-K0-0215 R:RULE-K0-0276#d X:BF-K0-0009#a | S: security findings M: MUST (P, R), X no modality E: OWASP category when applicable (all) T: none | labels: P EXTRA, R ORACLE_LINKED (whole record)
SPLIT R:RULE-K0-0281 | a: Layer status is PASS, FINDINGS, NOT APPLICABLE or NOT CHECKED; never PASS for an uninspected layer. | b: The scan completes only when applicable layers were inspected, findings carry evidence, uncertain findings are labelled and limitations stated.
SD P:RULE-K0-0522 R:RULE-K0-0281#a X:BF-K0-0009#b | S: security layer status M: MUST_NOT (P) = MUST + 'never' (R) (F7), X no modality E: none in any T: none
# r460-r470 .claude/skills/security-scan/references/scan-layers.md
RD EXAMPLE_GENERAL R:RULE-K0-0232 P:RULE-K0-0523 | P: no package upgrades during a scan unless asked.
